## 5. Actionable Recommendations for Manuscript Revisions

1. **Methods (§1.1 & §1.2 — Contamination Modeling):**
   Cite [`austin2023scrub`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/05_ecology_design/03_Austin_2023_SCRuBContaminantRemoval.pdf) and [`liu2022squeegee`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/05_ecology_design/02_Liu_2022_SqueegeeContamination.pdf). Explain that P4's spatial-recurrence admission criteria ($\ge 3$ variants, $\ge 3$ samples, $\ge 2$ sites) inherently avoids the severe over-subtraction documented by Austin et al. while confirming that MAG coverage tracks site geography rather than invariant kitome batches.
2. **Methods (§1.3 — Structural Gating):**
   Cite [`monzon2022folding`](file:///home/leechuck/Documents/papers/empty-quarter-mags/resources/literature/darkmatter-2026-10-13/papers/05_ecology_design/10_Monzon_2022_AntiFamAlphaFold.pdf) to justify excluding sequences $<100$ aa from fold-level novelty classifications, turning what could be seen as an arbitrary cutoff into a literature-backed protection against AlphaFold's false-confidence failure mode on short peptides.
